<!--
  com.apple.MobileGestalt.plist — HackiOS-begonia review skeleton
  ---------------------------------------------------------------
  Identity masqueraded: iPhone10,3 (iPhone X) · board D22AP · A11 Bionic ·
  chip-id 0x8020 = 32800 · running iOS 16.5 (Build 20F66).

  Real on-device caches store answers UNDER HASHED KEYS in a top-level
  `CacheExtra` dict (libMobileGestalt hashes the plain key and looks it up).
  The hashed names below are the verified values from
  theapplewiki.com/wiki/List_of_MobileGestalt_keys (plain names in comments).

  NOTE — keys from earlier project notes that do NOT exist in MobileGestalt:
    "HwModel"          → use HWModelStr  (hardware model, "D22AP") and
                         ProductType (device identifier "iPhone10,3")
    "MainScreenPitch"  → use main-screen-pitch (kebab, iOS7-era key names)
    "MainScreenWidth"  → use main-screen-width
  ChipID is written as the CPID as an INTEGER (Apple Wiki wording) = 32800;
  the string form "8020" is available via --chipid-repr hexstring on the
  generator.  Serial/ECID/UDID values are synthetic placeholders (UDID =
  SHA1 of the documented serial/ECID tuple); regenerate the file with
  ../patch_mobilegestalt.py instead of hand-editing.

  The canonical generator is ../patch_mobilegestalt.py — regenerate rather
  than hand-editing this file.  Screen numbers follow iPhone10,3 canonical
  geometry (1125×2436 @3x, 458 ppi; begonia's 1080×2340 panel is the same
  19.5:9 aspect ratio — see patch_mobilegestalt.py docstring).
-->
